const ESC_STRUCTURE_CONTENT = {
  "esc_vs_mined": "Most people think calcium is just calcium — a chalky mineral that sits in the stomach and slowly dissolves. ESC behaves nothing like that. Because it comes from a living biological structure, ESC interacts with the body in a way that feels natural, gentle, and efficient.\nThis is the same biological advantage built into CalPure, our ESC based calcium capsules now ready for customers who want a cleaner, more body friendly mineral source.\n\n### 🦴 A Biological Mineral Your Body Instantly Recognises\n\nESC comes from eggshell — a mineral structure nature designed to support life, not sit in rock for millions of years.\n- ESC behaves like a nutrient your body already understands ((esc_biological_calcium_identity))\n- Its biogenic origin makes it more compatible with human biology ((biogenic_calcium_source))\n- The mineral profile resembles food based calcium, not geological calcium ((food_like_mineral_behavior))\n- This natural familiarity is why ESC feels lighter and easier on digestion ((digestive_comfort_profile))\nESC is a biological calcium source — and your body responds to it as such.\n\n### 🧱 A Micro Porous Lattice That Opens Up Easily\n\nESC isn’t dense like rock calcium — it has a sponge like internal structure that helps it dissolve smoothly.\n- The eggshell contains a micro porous lattice with thousands of tiny channels ((micro_porous_lattice))\n- These pores allow water to enter quickly, improving breakdown ((enhanced_gastric_dissolution))\n- The increased surface area makes more calcium available for absorption ((surface_area_bioaccessibility_gain))\n- This is why ESC avoids the “chalky heaviness” people feel with traditional calcium ((low_density_digestive_behavior))\nESC opens up naturally — giving CalPure its clean, non chalky feel.\n\n### 🧬 A Mineral–Protein Matrix Built for Delivery\n\nESC doesn’t deliver calcium alone — it brings it in a natural complex your cells recognise.\n- Calcium is bound to proteins and collagen fragments in a mineral–protein matrix ((mineral_protein_matrix))\n- These bonds help guide calcium through your nutrient delivery pathways ((nutrient_delivery_pathways))\n- The structure forms bioavailable calcium complexes that cells can use efficiently ((bioavailable_calcium_complexes))\n- This natural packaging improves uptake without forcing the digestive system ((biological_uptake_support))\nESC delivers calcium in the same form nature intended — ready for use, not just swallowed.\n\n### 🟢 Outcome\n\nESC is biological, porous, and protein bound — a form of calcium your body can recognise, absorb, and use more naturally.\nCalPure simply carries this natural advantage forward, offering ESC in its cleanest, most intact form for everyday bone and joint support.",
  "esc_lattice": "ESC doesn’t behave like a solid mineral block — it behaves like a living structure. The eggshell’s internal lattice is the reason ESC feels lighter, dissolves better, and absorbs more naturally than rock based calcium.\nThis same natural architecture is what gives CalPure its clean, gentle mineral profile — a calcium source that feels like it belongs in the body, not on a geology shelf.\n\n### 🧱 A Sponge Like Internal Network Built by Nature\n\nESC is formed inside a living organism, not under geological pressure. That alone changes everything.\n- Thousands of micro channels create the ESC calcium lattice ((esc_calcium_lattice_structure))\n- These channels allow water to move through the mineral instantly ((hydration_channel_permeability))\n- The structure breaks apart smoothly instead of resisting digestion ((natural_lattice_disintegration_profile))\n- This prevents the dense, chalk like behaviour seen in rock calcium ((low_density_digestive_behavior))\nESC behaves like a mineral designed for biological use, not geological storage.\n\n### 💧 Porosity That Supports Fast, Comfortable Breakdown\n\nThe eggshell’s porous design wasn’t created for humans — it was created to support life inside the egg. But the body benefits from it too.\n- Water penetrates the lattice quickly, softening the mineral without harsh acidity ((rapid_gastric_penetration_dynamics))\n- The expanded surface area improves calcium release and availability ((surface_area_bioaccessibility_gain))\n- The structure avoids the “chalky lump” effect common with dense calcium tablets ((enhanced_gastric_dissolution))\n- This natural breakdown pattern supports smoother absorption in daily use ((biological_uptake_support))\nESC becomes usable calcium sooner — a quiet advantage built into CalPure’s formulation.\n\n### 🧬 A Lattice Designed for Mineral Delivery, Not Resistance\n\nThe eggshell lattice evolved to deliver minerals efficiently to growing life — a purpose that aligns surprisingly well with human digestion.\n- It supports natural mineral release patterns that match biological needs ((biological_mineral_release_mechanism))\n- The lattice interacts smoothly with human nutrient pathways ((biocompatible_lattice_interaction))\n- It forms mineral complexes that cells can recognise and utilise ((cell_friendly_mineral_complexing))\n- This compatibility reduces digestive strain and improves overall comfort ((digestive_comfort_profile))\nESC’s lattice isn’t random — it’s a biological design your body already understands.\n\n### 🟢 Outcome\n\nThe natural calcium lattice inside ESC makes it dissolve faster, absorb better, and feel lighter — giving your body a form of calcium that behaves like a nutrient, not a stone.\nThis is the structural advantage CalPure is built on: a mineral form that works with your biology, not against it.",
  "esc_microporous": "ESC’s micro porous structure isn’t a coincidence — it’s the result of biological engineering. An eggshell must protect life, breathe, exchange minerals, and still remain light enough for a bird to lay. That purpose shaped a calcium architecture completely different from the dense, geological minerals used in most supplements.\nThis same natural architecture is what makes CalPure dissolve smoothly, feel gentle on the stomach, and deliver calcium in a way the body can actually use.\n\n### 🧱 Nature Designed the Eggshell for Mineral Movement, Not Mineral Storage\n\nRock calcium forms under pressure and heat, becoming dense and resistant. ESC forms inside a living organism where minerals must move, exchange, and support growth.\n- The shell grows through a biological deposition process that creates thousands of micro channels ((biogenic_mineral_deposition_pattern))\n- These channels allow minerals and gases to pass between the shell and the developing embryo ((mineral_exchange_microchannels))\n- The structure must be strong yet permeable — a balance geology never needs to achieve ((strength_permeability_balance))\nESC’s architecture exists because life needed a mineral that could protect and deliver at the same time.\n\n### 💧 Porosity That Helps the Body, Not Just the Egg\n\nThe same porous design that supports an embryo also supports human digestion.\n- Water enters the lattice instantly, softening the mineral without harsh acidity ((rapid_hydration_response))\n- The expanded surface area increases contact with digestive fluids ((expanded_dissolution_interface))\n- This prevents the “chalky lump” effect common with dense calcium tablets ((anti_compaction_behavior))\n- The structure breaks down progressively, creating a smooth, comfortable digestive experience ((progressive_gastric_softening))\nESC dissolves the way a biological mineral should — gradually, evenly, and without heaviness.\n\n### 🧬 A Structure That Supports Natural Absorption Pathways\n\nBecause ESC is porous, it doesn’t overwhelm the digestive system with a sudden mineral load.\n- The lattice releases calcium in a controlled, biologically familiar pattern ((controlled_mineral_release_profile))\n- This aligns with how intestinal transporters naturally handle mineral uptake ((intestinal_transport_alignment))\n- The mineral–protein interactions inside ESC remain accessible during breakdown ((accessible_matrix_components))\n- The body receives calcium in a form closer to food than to stone ((food_mimicking_absorption_behavior))\nESC’s architecture works with the body’s rhythm instead of forcing it.\n\n### 🟢 Outcome\n\nESC has a micro porous architecture because nature built it for mineral exchange, not geological permanence.\nThis is why CalPure feels different from the moment it enters the stomach — it behaves like a living mineral, not a compressed rock.\nThe result is a calcium source that dissolves smoothly, absorbs efficiently, and supports the body with the same intelligence nature designed into the eggshell.",
  "esc_mineral_protein": "ESC is not just loose calcium powder. Inside the eggshell, calcium is woven into a living framework of proteins and collagen fragments — a mineral–protein matrix. This is one of the biggest reasons ESC behaves more like food than rock, and why CalPure feels so naturally compatible with the body.\n\n### 🧬  A Living Scaffold, Not a Dead Mineral\n\nIn nature, the eggshell is built as a structured composite, not a single mineral block.\n- Calcium crystals grow on a backbone of eggshell proteins and collagen like components ((matrix_scaffold_protein_backbone))\n- These proteins guide how minerals are laid down and organised ((protein_guided_mineral_orientation))\n- The result is a tightly integrated mineral–protein network, not loose, isolated particles ((integrated_mineral_protein_network))\n- This composite behaves more like a biological tissue than a geological deposit ((tissue_like_material_behavior))\nESC starts life as part of a living system — and it keeps that identity even when turned into a supplement.\n\n### 🔗 How Calcium Binds Into the Matrix\n\nThe way calcium attaches inside ESC changes how it behaves in the body.\n- Calcium ions interact with charged regions on matrix proteins ((ionic_binding_sites_engagement))\n- These interactions create stable but reversible mineral–protein bonds ((reversible_mineral_protein_linkages))\n- The matrix holds calcium in a semi structured, semi mobile state ((semi_structured_mineral_state))\n- This prevents the “hard, inert” behaviour seen in dense rock minerals ((reduced_inert_mineral_behavior))\nIn ESC, calcium is held, guided, and presented — not just dumped into the system.\n\n### 🍽️  Why ESC Behaves More Like Food Than Rock\n\nBecause calcium is embedded in a protein matrix, the body experiences ESC more like a nutrient than a raw mineral.\n- Digestive enzymes can interact with the protein components as they would with food ((enzyme_accessible_matrix_regions))\n- As proteins are broken down, they gradually release bound calcium ((digestion_coupled_mineral_release))\n- This couples mineral availability to normal digestive processes ((physiological_release_synchronisation))\n- The experience is closer to eating a mineral rich food than swallowing a chalk tablet ((food_mimicking_intake_experience))\nESC fits into the body’s existing digestion logic — it doesn’t force a new one.\n\n### 🚚  A Matrix That Supports Downstream Utilisation\n\nThe mineral–protein matrix doesn’t just affect digestion — it also influences how calcium is used.\n- Matrix fragments can help keep calcium in a more soluble, bioavailable form ((matrix_assisted_solubility_support))\n- This supports smoother passage through the intestinal environment ((intestinal_phase_stability))\n- The structured release reduces the chance of large, unmanageable mineral spikes ((controlled_bioavailability_profile))\n- Overall, the body gets calcium in a form it can recognise, process, and direct where needed ((biologically_coordinated_utilisation))\nThis is one of the quiet reasons CalPure feels efficient — it delivers calcium in a guided, not chaotic, way.\n\n### 🟢  Outcome\n\nESC forms a natural mineral–protein matrix where calcium is embedded, guided, and gradually released — not just present as an inert rock.\nCalPure preserves this matrix based identity, offering calcium in a form that behaves like a nutrient from food: structured, compatible, and naturally aligned with how the body prefers to receive minerals."
};

