const ESC_PURITY_PROCESSING_CONTENT = {
  "esc_purity_safety": "Calcium can come from two very different worlds:\nthe geological world (rocks, quarries, industrial mining)\nand the biological world (eggshells — a food grade, naturally filtered mineral source).\nESC belongs to the second world.\nAnd that single difference changes everything about purity, safety, and biological compatibility.\nESC is not scraped from the earth.\nIt is grown inside a living system, protected by membranes, filtered by biology, and free from the contaminants that commonly affect mined calcium.\n\n### 🧩 1. ESC Comes from a Food Grade Biological Source — Not the Ground\n\nMined calcium (carbonate, dolomite, limestone) comes from geological deposits that may contain:\n- heavy metals\n- industrial pollutants\n- soil borne contaminants\n- environmental residues\nESC, by contrast:\n- originates from a food regulated supply chain\n- is naturally filtered by the hen’s biological system\n- contains calcium in a biogenic mineral form ((biogenic_mineral_profile))\nThis makes ESC inherently cleaner before processing even begins.\n\n### 🧼 2. ESC Avoids the Heavy Metal Risks Found in Mined Calcium\n\nGeological minerals often contain trace amounts of:\n- lead\n- arsenic\n- cadmium\n- mercury\nThese must be aggressively purified — and even then, residues can remain.\nESC avoids this risk because:\n- eggshells do not accumulate heavy metals the way rocks do\n- the biological system regulates mineral deposition\n- ESC starts with naturally low contaminant levels\nThis is why ESC consistently tests cleaner than mined calcium sources.\n\n### 🧪 3. ESC Requires Minimal Processing — Mined Calcium Requires Harsh Treatment\n\nTo make mined calcium safe, manufacturers must use:\n- high temperature calcination\n- acid washing\n- chemical purification\n- mechanical grinding of rock\nESC requires:\n- gentle cleaning\n- controlled low temperature processing\n- preservation of its natural ((biological_mineral_structure))\nLess processing = fewer contaminants introduced = cleaner final ingredient.\n\n### 🛡️ 4. ESC Retains Its Natural Mineral–Protein Matrix, Which Protects Purity\n\nESC is not just calcium — it contains a mineral–protein matrix that:\n- stabilises the mineral\n- supports ((matrix_assisted_solubility_support))\n- reduces the need for chemical additives\n- keeps the ingredient closer to its natural state\nMined calcium has no such matrix and must rely on industrial processing to achieve stability.\n🌱 5. ESC Is Sustainably Sourced and Traceable\nMined calcium:\n- requires quarrying\n- disrupts land\n- produces dust and waste\n- has variable traceability\nESC:\n- comes from an existing food stream\n- uses a by product that would otherwise be discarded\n- is fully traceable from farm to finished ingredient\n- aligns with clean label and sustainability expectations\nClean source → clean processing → clean final mineral.\n\n### 🟢 Outcome\n\nESC is cleaner than mined calcium because it begins as a biological, food grade mineral, not a geological rock.\nIt avoids heavy metals, requires minimal processing, retains its natural mineral–protein matrix, and comes from a sustainable, traceable source.\nThe result is a purer, safer, more biologically aligned calcium that fits modern expectations for clean nutrition.",
  "esc_low_temperature_processing": "Low temperature processing is one of the most important reasons ESC performs better than conventional calcium ingredients.\nWhere mined calcium must be blasted, burned, acid washed, or calcined at extreme temperatures, ESC is processed gently — preserving its biogenic mineral structure, its natural protein mineral matrix, and its biological compatibility.\n\n### 🔥 1. High Heat Processing Destroys Mineral Structure — ESC Avoids This Completely\n\nMost mined calcium sources undergo:\n- 800–1000°C calcination\n- acid purification\n- mechanical grinding\n- thermal sterilisation\nThese steps strip away natural structure and leave behind a harsh, chalk like mineral.\nESC avoids this because it is processed at controlled low temperatures, preserving:\n- ((biogenic_mineral_profile))\n- ((biological_mineral_structure))\n- ((matrix_assisted_solubility_support))\nThis keeps ESC closer to its natural, food grade state.\n\n### 🧬 2. Low Temperature Processing Preserves the Mineral–Protein Matrix\n\nESC is not just calcium — it contains a natural mineral–protein matrix that improves solubility, absorption, and biological behaviour.\nHigh heat would destroy this matrix.\nOur low temperature method protects it, allowing ESC to retain:\n- its gentle dissolution behaviour\n- its food like absorption pattern\n- its compatibility with collagen rich tissues\nThis matrix is a major reason ESC outperforms rock based calcium.\n\n### 💧 3. Low Temperature Processing Maintains ESC’s Gentle Dissolution Profile\n\nESC dissolves gradually in our body— not explosively like carbonate, and not aggressively like citrate.\nThis gentle behaviour depends on its natural structure.\nLow temperature processing preserves:\n- ((stepwise_mineral_release))\n- ((circulatory_stability_support))\n- ((target_tissue_mineral_availability))\nThis ensures ESC enters the body in a calm, controlled way that supports bone, joint, and cartilage tissues.\n\n### 🛡️ 4. Low Temperature Processing Protects Purity\n\nHigh heat and chemical processing can introduce:\n- residues\n- contaminants\n- structural distortions\nESC avoids these risks because our process:\n- uses minimal intervention\n- preserves natural purity\n- maintains food grade safety\n- avoids chemical harshness\nThis is why ESC consistently tests cleaner than mined calcium.\n\n### 🧩 5. Low Temperature Processing Preserves ESC’s Biological Compatibility\n\nThe body recognises ESC as a biological mineral, not a geological one.\nThis recognition depends on its natural structure — which only survives gentle processing.\nOur method preserves:\n- ((biogenic_mineral_profile))\n- ((biological_mineral_structure))\n- ((osteoblast_ready_mineral_form))\nThis makes ESC easier for the body to absorb, transport, and use.\n\n### 🟢 Outcome\n\nLow temperature processing protects ESC’s purity, structure, and biological behaviour.\nIt preserves the mineral–protein matrix, maintains gentle dissolution, avoids contamination, and keeps ESC in the natural form the body recognises and uses most efficiently.\nThis is not just a manufacturing choice — it is a scientific advantage that directly improves ESC’s performance in bone, joint, and collagen matrix health."
};

